{"name":"Third Eye Chakra","hex":"#243bcd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"third","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["The ordinal form of the cardinal number three; Coming after the second."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The person or thing in the third position.","One of three equal parts of a whole."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/third"},{"term":"eye","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An organ through which animals see (“perceive surroundings via light”).","The visual sense."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To carefully or appraisingly observe (someone or something).","To consider."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eye"},{"term":"chakra","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of (at least) seven centres of spiritual energy in or near the body, according to Ayurveda philosophy.","Synonym of hackery."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chakra"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ajna","blocks":[{"text":"Ajna, brow or third eye chakra, is the sixth primary chakra in the body according to Hindu yogic traditions and signifies the unconscious mind, the direct link to Brahman. The third eye is said to connect people to their intuition, give them the ability to communicate with the world, or help them receive messages from the past and the future."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Chakra6.svg/330px-Chakra6.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ajna"},{"title":"Third eye","blocks":[{"text":"The third eye is an intangible eye, usually depicted as located on the forehead, supposed to provide perception beyond ordinary sight. In Hinduism, the third eye refers to the ajna chakra. In both Hinduism and Buddhism, the third eye is said to be located around the middle of the forehead, slightly above the junction of the eyebrows, representing the enlightenment one achieves through meditation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Shiva_Mus%C3%A9e_Guimet_22971.jpg/330px-Shiva_Mus%C3%A9e_Guimet_22971.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_eye"},{"title":"Eye","blocks":[{"text":"An eye is a sensory organ that allows an organism to perceive visual information. It detects light and converts it into electro-chemical impulses in neurons (neurones). It is part of an organism's visual system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Krilleyekils.jpg/330px-Krilleyekils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye"},{"title":"Chakra","blocks":[{"text":"A chakra is a meditation-aid in the form of a psychic or psychospiritual energy-center in the subtle body, as visualized in a variety of Hindu and Buddhist tantric yoga and meditation practices."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chakra"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Buddha_Victoria_%26_Albert.jpg/500px-Buddha_Victoria_%26_Albert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Buddha_Victoria_%26_Albert.jpg/1280px-Buddha_Victoria_%26_Albert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Buddha_Victoria_%26_Albert.jpg/500px-Buddha_Victoria_%26_Albert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Buddha with an urna","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABuddha_Victoria_%26_Albert.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bison_bonasus_right_eye_close-up.jpg/500px-Bison_bonasus_right_eye_close-up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https:/